course: dictionary
lesson: 4705
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Honeypot is one of them. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning is right. «Winnie-the-Pooh keeps his honey in a honeypot.» Here a honeypot is a pot for keeping honey.
explain: «The old town is a tourist honeypot, so the streets are busy all summer.» Here honeypot is an informal way of saying a place that attracts lots of people, like bees to honey. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: a crowded town fits, but a pot of honey does not.
explain: In computing, a honeypot is a trap. It pretends to be an easy target so that hackers are caught. The meaning is different again, so you must always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Honeypot has more than one meaning, so use the context to choose the right one.
fact: «Honeypot» can mean a pot for keeping honey.
fact: Informally, a «tourist honeypot» is a place that attracts lots of visitors, like bees to honey.
fact: In computing, a honeypot is a trap set up to catch hackers by pretending to be an easy target.
fact: Honeypot ants are real insects. Some workers store sweet liquid in their swollen bellies, and they hang from the nest roof as living food stores.
exercise: «Winnie-the-Pooh keeps his honey in a honeypot.» What does honeypot mean here? | A trap for hackers | *A pot for keeping honey | A bee's nest | A crowded holiday place
exercise: In geography, a «honeypot site» is: | A kind of honey | *A popular place that gets crowded with visitors | A sweet shop by the sea | A quiet forest with no paths
exercise: «Honeypot ants turn some workers into living jars of sweet liquid.» What do these workers store? | Stones for building | Water from rain | *Sweet liquid | Seeds for winter
test: «Some honeypot ant workers swell with sweet liquid and hang from the nest roof, storing food for hard times.» Why do the workers store sweet liquid? | To attract tourists | *For hard times, as food | To make the nest look pretty | To catch hackers
test: In computing, what is a honeypot? | A fast computer game | *A trap that pretends to be an easy target to catch hackers | A pot on a computer desk for sticky honey | A website for holiday bookings
exam: «The beach is a tourist honeypot in August.» What does honeypot mean here? | A pot of honey on the sand | A trap for hackers | *A place that attracts lots of people | A kind of ant
